  "id": "COMPOUND:28862 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Dendocarbin K appears to have a shared target relationship with SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. All of these compounds are implicated in targeting HCC1937, suggesting a potential pathway where Dendocarbin K may act through a common mechanism that influences the activity of these compounds against HCC1937. The evidence points to a possible role for Dendocarbin K in modulating the biological response of SNU-387, which in turn affects HCC1937. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential dependency on SNU-387 as a mediator, with Dendocarbin K possibly acting through a mechanism that enhances or alters the activity of these targets. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
